[[File:Greater_coat_of_arms_of_the_United_States.svg|thumb|The coat of arms of the United States featuring a '''bald eagle''']]
{{wikispecies|Haliaeetus leucocephalus}}

===Etymology===
Named after the white markings on its head and tail.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q127216}}{{taxfmt|Haliaeetus leucocephalus|species}}, a species of [[eagle]] native to North America and notable for the white [[plumage]] on its head.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|American eagle}}, {{l|en|bald erne}}, {{l|en|baldie}}

